_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T12:45:14Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T12:45:39Z","body":"> This implementation leans towards the existing Godot string formatting patterns, such as removing trailing 0's in floats\r\n\r\nWe actually changed the behavior recently in String to include trailing `.0` when printing and stringifying floats.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906814233/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907230859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103732#issuecomment-2907230859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103732","id":2907230859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tSNKL","user":{"login":"mpsalisbury","id":91654,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNjU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91654?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury","html_url":"https://github.com/mpsalisbury","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpsalisbury/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T22:28:52Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T22:28:52Z","body":"> > This implementation leans towards the existing Godot string formatting patterns, such as removing trailing 0's in floats\r\n> \r\n> We actually changed the behavior recently in String to include trailing `.0` when printing and stringifying floats.\r\n\r\nThis comment was referring to the logic that removes extra trailing zeroes after the first to the right of the decimal. e.g. \"4.000\" -> \"4.0\". \r\n\r\nBut thinking about this more I've realized that that behavior isn't appropriate here. If somebody is explicitly asking for two decimals, they want two even if they're zeroes. So I've updated the logic to include all digits when the precision is explicitly specified. Corresponding tests are added too.\r\n\r\nThanks for the comment.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907230859/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5043717059","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103732#issuecomment-5043717059","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/